<title>USA: Bids for U.S. lead range $0.3100-$0.3625/lb.</title>
<headline>Bids for U.S. lead range $0.3100-$0.3625/lb.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-10-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bids for surplus U.S. lead ranged from $0.3100 to $0.3625 per pound at a monthly bid opening Thursday, the Defense National Stockpile Center said.</p>
<p>Hirsch Metals Corp was high bidder, bidding $0.3625 per pound for 20 tonnes of lead.</p>
<p>Seven firms bid for a total of 2,289 tonnes of lead.</p>
<p>The agency usually announces awards the day after the bid opening.</p>
<p>-- Washington Commodities Desk (202) 898-8489</p>
